         Dog Registration   Oreo is excited to let you know that the 2026 dog licenses will be available starting December 16, 2025!     I am excited to announce the new shape of this year’s license.  At the end of the 2024/2025 School Year, I had the privilege of visiting with all the 5th Graders across our three elementary schools.  We discussed civics, what a Town Clerk does, and the importance of voting.  We also took a vote on what the shape of the 2025 dog license would be.  The options they had to choose from were a bell, a heart, a pentagon, and a tear drop.    Bell won with 44% of the vote!    I had a great time with the kids and I look forward to next year’s Dog Tag Election. 2026 Dog Tags:  Dog Licenses cover a calendar year and are  due annually in January .  Intact dogs are $20.00 Neutered/Spayed dogs are $15.00.   If you have a new dog or if the rabies certificate you previously provided has expired, please provide the current certificate when registering. If this is your first time registering your dog after spaying or neutering, please provided the pertinent paperwork. Dogs licensed after  May 31st  will be subject to a $50.00 late fee, per dog (in addition to the regular registration fee).  Dogs licensed after  June 30th  will be subject to a $50.00 Noncriminal Disposition Fee, per dog (in addition to the $50.00 late fee, and the regular registration fee).    Please take advantage of one of the three ways you can license your dog(s). In Person: Cash or Check made out to the TOWN OF SHARON The Town Clerk’s Office is open:   M,T,W:      8:00am - 5:00pm Thursday: 8:00am - 6:00pm Friday:      8:00am - 12:30pm Online:  Click Here Mail: Follow the instructions on the form attached to the bottom of your annual census (Mailed to you in January). Kennel Licenses : Kennel Licenses are required for certain dog related businesses and anyone who personally owns five or more dogs.    All kennel licenses are required to pass inspection by the Animal Control Officer  BEFORE  a license is granted (M.G.L Ch. 140 Section  137A  and  137C ).  An application for a kennel license can be picked up at the Town Clerk’s Office or you can  Click Here .   If you own a business that works with dogs, you may be required to purchase a kennel license.  Please contact the Animal Control Officer at 781-784-1513 to inquire about the regulations.   Kennel licenses are: $35.00 for 1 to 4 dogs $60.00 for 5 to 10 dogs $125.00 for 11+ dogs 
     

 
